       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is double the 3200 mg/day maximum in the prescribing labeling for ibuprofen. Doses above that increase the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, cardiovascular events, and fluid retention, even with normal baseline function.\n\nCommon regimens that stay within the limit include:\n- 800 mg PO every 6 hours (3200 mg/day), or\n- 1200 mg PO every 6 hours (4800 mg/day), if you intend a higher dose for a specific indication and accept the added risk, though this exceeds the labeled maximum.\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose and frequency. Once you do, I'll enter the order. If 1600 mg QID was intentional, tell me so and I'll enter it as written with a note documenting the rationale."
